        <h1 id="page-heading">Puritan Test</h1>
      </div>

      <div id="page-center">
        <div id="page-left">&nbsp;</div>
        <div id="page-right">&nbsp;</div>

        <div id="page-content">
          <span class="flavortext">
            <p>We must endeavor foremost to follow that which is entirely Puritan in character. Else, we are no better than Wilhelmina W. Witchiepoo or other sinners.</p>
          </span>
          
          <ol>
            <li>What be the correct show of devotion to the LORD?
            <ol style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
              <li>Hands folded at bowed head</li>
              <li>Rapt, oiled torso writhing</li>
              <li>Whispering in obscure profanities</li>
            </ol></li>
            <li>Which maketh the finest hair shirt? 
            <ol style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
              <li>Stinging ant mesh</li>
              <li>Squash and turnip strands</li>
              <li>Two pair otter pelts</li>
            </ol></li>
            <li>Filleth the blank: "Goody Wright ____ to the Devil!"
            <ol style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
              <li>Art unnaturally akin</li> 
              <li>Ain't too averse</li>
              <li>Doth turn her soul over</li>
            </ol></li>
            <li>What doth this picture suggest?<br/>
            <img src="puritan_test.jpg" />
            <ol style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
              <li>An earthly delight</li>
              <li>Thanksgiving feast nap swoon</li>
              <li>Pain, tragedy, and giant birds</li>
            </ol></li>
            <li>Jabots - how poofy is TOO poofy?
            <ol style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
              <li>Two pleats should be apt enough</li>
              <li>Hills of frills! Lakes of lace! With floral print rims!</li>
              <li>Fanciful neckwear means ruin, whatever the style</li>
            </ol></li>
            <li>Be thou sinful?
            <ol style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
              <li>Part of me is naughty</li>
              <li>Is this query or trap, rather?</li>
              <li>Regularly as rain each April</li>
            </ol></li>
            <li>Thy neighbor's child is possessed. How should he be exorcised?
            <ol style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
              <li>Tar and feathers</li>
              <li>Bible raised high, rant thunderingly of the LORD's power</li>
              <li>Nutria hair on the abdomen - marvelous against ye olde spin-and-spew</li>
            </ol></li>
            <li>Hast thou ever "Smacked the flapjack?"
            <ol style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
              <li>My motto: do it every day for good health</li>
              <li>No, the spattered paint really makes a mess (I'm told)</li>
              <li>'Tis difficult to train each waterfowl (I'm told)</li>
            </ol></li>
          </ol>
        </div><!--end of id="page-content"-->
      </div><!--end of id="page-center"-->

